        "original_id": "efb6aa3f-7208-5ab9-9d16-eb730f963a80",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hong Kong, Diamond Hill, Lantau Island, Ngong Ping\n- Organizations: Chi Lin Nunnery, Po Lin Monastery\n- Products: Tian Tan Buddha\n- Topics: Buddhist temples, tourist attractions\n\nFacts:\n- Chi Lin Nunnery is a prominent Buddhist temple in Diamond Hill, Hong Kong, and it was built in the Tang Dynasty architectural style.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is a large bronze statue of Buddha Shakyamuni in Ngong Ping on Lantau Island, Hong Kong, and it was completed in 1993.\n- Po Lin Monastery is a prominent Buddhist temple on Lantau Island, Hong Kong.\n- Po Lin Monastery is famous for the outdoor bronze statue Tian Tan Buddha.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is also known as the Big Buddha.\n- Tian Tan Buddha attracts many visitors during weekends and holidays.\n- Ngong Ping 360 is home to both Po Lin Monastery and Tian Tan Buddha, which are already major tourist attractions.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
